data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` with `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** Both work as expected:

```csharp
Span<nint>  signedSpan   = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsignedSpan = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

These compile and run without requiring an `unsafe` context (since they assign directly to a `Span<T>`). On this 64-bit system, `nint` is 8 bytes. This has been supported since C# 9 / .NET 5, when `nint`/`nuint` were introduced as first-class unmanaged types eligible for `stackalloc`.
